The '''Corpse''' is a new floor added in [[The Binding of Isaac: Repentance]], which acts as the {{s|Womb}}'s alternative Chapter. It features a desolate and dreary atmosphere with enemies that carry the theme of death and advanced rot. The Corpse is one of five final levels in The Binding of Isaac, alongside the {{s|Chest}}, the {{s|Dark Room}}, {{dlc|a+}} {{s|The Void}}, and {{dlc|r}} {{s|Home}}. Like in the Womb and its alternate floors, floors in Corpse do not naturally generate item rooms or shops, and all damage taken will do a full heart of damage to Isaac's HP (unless he has {{i|The Wafer}}), regardless of the source.

To access The Corpse, the player must first open the flesh door at the end of the {{s|Mausoleum}}/{{s|Gehenna}} II after defeating the Mausoleum version of [[Mom#Behaviour in Mausoleum/Gehenna|Mom]] by doing one of the following:
* Collect {{I|Knife Piece 1}} and {{I|Knife Piece 2}}, which are obtained via puzzles inside {{s|Downpour}} and the {{s|Mines}}, to build the knife familiar, and stab the door with it.
* Sacrifice one key and open the door by using {{I|Sharp Key}}.
* {{I|Cracked Orb}} can also open the door while simultaneously letting you keep the knife familiar.
* Using a {{p|Soul of Cain}}.
* If Isaac exits the {{r|Boss Rush}} room in Gehenna after 25 minutes have passed, there is a chance that the flesh door will change positions to the wall where the boss rush door was, causing Isaac to "come out" of the flesh door and leaving it open, allowing entry without the knife.

On the other side of the flesh door, the player will fight the Mausoleum version of [[Mom's Heart#Behaviour in Mausoleum/Gehenna|Mom's Heart]], after which the entrance to the Womb will turn into the Corpse entrance, which will take the player into the Corpse floor.

The boss of Corpse II is always {{e|Mother}}.

