== Notes ==
* {{I|Mama Mega!|dlc=x}} can not be used to open the Flesh Door.
* {{i|We Need To Go Deeper!}} and {{p|Ehwaz}} cannot generate trapdoors in Corpse II.<br>An {{r|I AM ERROR}} room can only be visited in Corpse II via clipping out of a {{r|Crawl Space}}; such an I AM ERROR room will contain a passageway which leads back to the starting room of the floor.
* If the game is exited after defeating {{e|Mother}} and rejoined, there will be a door in the room allowing the player to leave the room. This can be used to go to a {{r|Sacrifice Room}} and then warp to the {{s|Dark Room}}, letting the run continue further.
* {{dlc|r+}} If the player has previously defeated {{e|Mother}}, beating her again will cause a portal leading to {{s|The Void}} to spawn, allowing the player to continue their run without the need for a sacrifice room.

== Trivia ==
* The Corpse is the only Alternative Chapter to not have any alternative floors.
** An unused floor named Mortis, presumably as an alternative to the Corpse, exists in the game files.
* In ''Antibirth'', the hole to the Mother battle had 4 {{e|Locked Chest}}s next to it that always contained items, similar to chests in {{s|Chest}}.
* If a room's floor is filled with blood, there will be a huge blood stain on the floor upon entering any room adjacent to it.

== Music ==
* The music for Corpse is titled ''Carrion''.<ref>[https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/album/the-binding-of-isaac-repentance-ost ''The Binding of Isaac: Repentance'' OST]</ref>
** The term "carrion" refers to the decaying flesh of dead animals.

